# Preview Secret Configuration
#
# The Studio builds "Open Preview" links as:
#   {SANITY_STUDIO_PRODUCTION_URL}/api/draft?secret={SANITY_STUDIO_PREVIEW_SECRET}&slug=...
#
# The web app's /api/draft route validates that secret against its own
# SANITY_PREVIEW_SECRET. The two MUST hold the same value, and there is no
# fallback on either side — if unset, preview links are hidden and the route
# returns 503.
#
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -base64 32
#
# SECURITY: `sanity build` compiles every SANITY_STUDIO_* variable into the
# PUBLIC Studio JavaScript bundle. Anyone who can load the Studio URL can read
# this secret, so treat it as "keeps drafts out of search engines and casual
# visitors", not as strong access control. For real protection, migrate to
# next-sanity's defineEnableDraftMode + @sanity/preview-url-secret, which
# validates a per-session secret stored in the dataset instead.

# --- Local development ---
# Put the REAL value in .env.development.local (gitignored), NOT in
# .env.development (tracked in git).
SANITY_STUDIO_PREVIEW_SECRET=replace-me-with-a-random-32-byte-secret
SANITY_STUDIO_PRODUCTION_URL=http://localhost:3001

# --- Deployed Studio (dppadmin.sanity.studio) ---
# Set in apps/studio/.env.production, which is gitignored:
# SANITY_STUDIO_PROJECT_ID=as5tildt
# SANITY_STUDIO_DATASET=production
# SANITY_STUDIO_PREVIEW_SECRET=[same value as the web app's SANITY_PREVIEW_SECRET]
# SANITY_STUDIO_PRODUCTION_URL=https://digiprint-main-web.netlify.app
